  "aciklama": "On June 15, 1904, the steamboat General Slocum burned in New York Harbor. Its life preservers were rotten and weighted with iron; its lifeboats were wired in place. The failure mechanism: safety equipment that passed inspection but did not work.\n\nFailure chain: Fire starts in storage room → Rotten 13-year-old life preservers → Some weighted with iron to pass → Lifeboats wired to the deck → Inspection had passed it all\n\nAnother reconstruction: The Disaster That Ended the Age of the Airship — https://youtu.be/PGOKZhPYo7c\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"PS General Slocum, East River.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PS_General_Slocum%2C_East_River.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Among the oil barrels where fire started, showing defective life preservers and life boats. General Slocum Disaster, New York Harbor, June 15, 1904 LCCN2009632218.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Among_the_oil_barrels_where_fire_started%2C_showing_defective_life_preservers_and_life_boats._General_Slocum_Disaster%2C_New_York_Harbor%2C_June_15%2C_1904_LCCN2009632218.jpg\n• Archival film: \"The mass of burned timbers and ruined metal, showing broken paddle wheels s(h)a(f)t. General Slocum Disaster, New York Harbor, June 15, 1904 LCCN2009632219.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_mass_of_burned_timbers_and_ruined_metal%2C_showing_broken_paddle_wheels_s(h)a(f)t._General_Slocum_Disaster%2C_New_York_Harbor%2C_June_15%2C_1904_LCCN2009632219.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Stern view of the Slocum. What was left of the boat which had on board over 1400 people. General Slocum Disaster, June 15, 1904 LCCN2009632222.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stern_view_of_the_Slocum._What_was_left_of_the_boat_which_had_on_board_over_1400_people._General_Slocum_Disaster%2C_June_15%2C_1904_LCCN2009632222.jpg\n• Archival film: \"All that was left of the boat which carried over 1000 souls to destruction. General view of Slocum after being raised, Slocum Disaster, New York Harbor LCCN2009632223.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:All_that_was_left_of_the_boat_which_carried_over_1000_souls_to_destruction._General_view_of_Slocum_after_being_raised%2C_Slocum_Disaster%2C_New_York_Harbor_LCCN2009632223.jpg\n• Archival film: \"PS General Slocum, sinking.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PS_General_Slocum%2C_sinking.jpg\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — PS General Slocum — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PS_General_Slocum\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\n#shorts #engineering #maritime",
